{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: a merge receipt must not time out on a healthy resident.\n\nhugh asked on 2026-10-16 why landing in the artroom workroom still takes so long, and approved filing this.\n\nOn 2026-10-16, the replay of artroom's 58-successor landing on a frozen copy (depth 43,744) moved main and then failed with \"record merge succession: batch submit: Post http://127.0.0.1:7795/v0/submit: context deadline exceeded … the resident had 10s to answer and did not.\" The receipt did not land in the copy. While the receipt was submitted, the resident's sampled stacks showed about 30 s in workroom foldState.append staleness: stalenessScope.successionCondemned, mergeSuccessionPlan and foldState.publishedByMerge, reached from unsettledCommitmentEvents. That part is only partly measured, because the sampler saw only the HTTP goroutines. The default submit deadline is 10 s. A merge whose receipt times out leaves the target moved with no durable receipt, so the actor has to resume it by hand. The artroom audit asserts on 2026-10-16 describe original gs merge processes still running long after the merge commit existed.\n\nOutcome. First measure where a resident spends its time appending a large merge receipt and its succession acts. Then make that append fast enough to finish well inside the default deadline at this depth, or make the merge path itself wait for the receipt as long as it needs, with a stated bound. A merge that has moved its target must never be left without its receipt by a client timeout alone.","body":{"conditions":"1. The report states the measured resident time to append the receipt and the first successor of the artroom 58-successor landing on a frozen copy, before and after, with the profile that located the cost. 2. On that copy, gs land completes the receipt and its whole succession without a deadline error at the default settings. 3. If the fix is in the fold's append path, the projection it produces is byte-identical to before at the same frontier (compare whole projection dumps on a frozen copy); if it is a deadline change for the merge path, the bound is stated in docs/reference/gs/merge.md and land.md. 4. A test pins the chosen behaviour. 5. go test ./... passes at the head.","target_head":"5876d2118fa3d9d223dfc923744bc0bb9ef1dfc0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}